BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (UFS2 has a superblock, cylinder groups and inodes analogous in purpose to UFS1, but the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (on-disk inode structure is different. UFS2 stores larger block addresses and extended) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (metadata, enabling increased file and volume capacities. A valid reader must parse the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (format version and its exact inode fields instead of casting a UFS1 disk inode to a UFS2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (structure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Each cylinder group maintains block/inode allocation metadata and locality information.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (Data blocks can be divided into fragments. Extended attributes may be associated with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (separately allocated blocks, and their allocation/deallocation dependencies have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (implications for consistency. Updated timestamp structures and inode metadata were explicit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 514.0 Tm (design goals.) Tj ET
