BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (Cylinder-group placement strategies aim to keep related data near its inode and disperse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (directories sufficiently for balance. Bitmaps and summary counts permit efficient) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (free-space selection. Direct and indirect block pointers map the file into allocated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (storage. As with UFS1, the exact algorithm used by the operating system is a policy layered) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (on the persistent format.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Directory entries carry inode references, record lengths and names. Hard links, ownership,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (permissions and other Unix behaviour require consistent inode metadata. UFS2's metadata) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (structures support extended attributes, and directory or inode corruption must be handled) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (with format-specific bounds and revision awareness.) Tj ET
