BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (UFS2 participates in BSD's soft-updates model, which tracks write dependencies and enforces) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (an order that avoids certain inconsistent allocation states without requiring every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (metadata write to be synchronous. Soft updates do not journal all file data. Some) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (deployments may use a journaled variant or soft-updates journalling, but the presence and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (policy must be discovered rather than assumed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (The 2003 engineering work addressed extended attribute dependencies, cleaner free-space) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (accounting and scalable recovery operations. Offline fsck remains important when metadata) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (is damaged. A modern repair tool checks group data, ownership maps, extended metadata and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (directory connectivity instead of treating a consistent superblock as a complete audit.) Tj ET
